&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191820/rss" title="furifont.antfu.me" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Furifont: A Japanese Font That Draws Its Own Furigana&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Furigana, the small readings above kanji, usually mean using &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ruby&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; markup or JavaScript. Anthony's font does it with OpenType features alone! &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191821/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Repo here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthony Fu &lt;/p&gt;
