&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191535/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1791980846/dwgixdfnss8se8vv6o8n.png" width="640" style="      line-height: 100%;  "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191535/rss" title="videojs.org" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1.25em; font-weight: 400;"&gt;What the iPhone Duo Means for Web Development&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — The &lt;em&gt;Duo&lt;/em&gt; is out next week, so Darius fired up the simulator to try the Device Posture and Viewport Segments APIs (both available behind a flag). Using Video.js components and CSS, he tried to recreate Netflix's folded-player UI, but Apple's fullscreen restrictions made things a tad interesting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Darius Cepulis (Video.js) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191536/rss" title="lea.verou.me" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The Best Way to Use Icons in Web UIs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Lea shows how to insert and tweak icons without touching &lt;em&gt;any&lt;/em&gt; HTML, using &lt;code&gt;--icon&lt;/code&gt; custom properties, &lt;code&gt;@property&lt;/code&gt;, style queries, and &lt;code&gt;mask&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191573/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The result?&lt;/a&gt; A pure CSS icon system that’s “&lt;em&gt;more flexible and maintainable than what you've been using&lt;/em&gt;”.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lea Verou &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191534/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/dd0bc385.png" width="135" height="135" style="padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px;     line-height: 100%; "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191534/rss" title="master.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Become the TypeScript Expert on Your Team&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Be the person your team trusts to review AI-generated TypeScript. Learn generics, conditional types, and discriminated unions in depth, then use that knowledge to catch subtle errors and steer AI toward cleaner types.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Master.dev &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191537/rss" title="interop-rank.fxdx.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The 2027 Web Platform Feature Ranking Returns&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Back for a second year, Firefox's ranker lets you sign in with GitHub, compare and rank the Interop 2027 proposals. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191538/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Jake Archibald says&lt;/a&gt; last year’s findings (taken from ~1,900 rankings) helped “&lt;em&gt;prioritise a lot of work this year”&lt;/em&gt;, so it's worth having your say.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Firefox &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;"&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;⚡️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;IN BRIEF&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📊 The &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191539/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;results of the 2026 &lt;em&gt;Stack Overflow&lt;/em&gt; Developer Survey&lt;/a&gt; are out. With over 30,000 responses, JavaScript came in as #1 language for the 12th year in a row.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🦊 Mozilla now &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191540/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;offers an &lt;em&gt;Enterprise&lt;/em&gt; version&lt;/a&gt; of Firefox, &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191541/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;focusing on things&lt;/a&gt; like compliance, regulatory requirements, security, and telemetry controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔒 Starting February next year &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191542/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;all new/renewed Let's Encrypt certificates will use a 64 day lifetime&lt;/a&gt; by default (down from 90).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧭 Apple has &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191543/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;shared a new page making their case&lt;/a&gt; for switching over from Chrome to Safari.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🛡️ If you miss Arc, &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191544/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Crest is a new browser hoping to scratch a similar itch&lt;/a&gt;. It curiously offers both Chromium and WebKit rendering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;📙&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;"&gt;Articles, Opinions &amp;amp; Tutorials&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191545/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1791983278/nahlayibmp2hhjswdnlk.png" width="640" style="    line-height: 100%;      "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191545/rss" title="calibreapp.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Lazy Loading Images and Media: How Far Ahead Browsers Fetch&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Ben measures how far ahead Chrome, Firefox and Safari fetch lazy-loaded media. He also shares &lt;em&gt;what&lt;/em&gt; we can lazy load (including video and audio in Chromium browsers), and covers where &lt;code&gt;lazy&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;eager&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;fetchpriority&lt;/code&gt; fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ben Schwarz (Calibre) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191546/rss" title="sindresorhus.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;How Sindre Sorhus' Personal Site is Now Made in &lt;em&gt;Swift&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A prolific JavaScript developer explains why he dropped Astro and now builds his personal site, styling and markup included, with Apple's Swift language.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sindre Sorhus &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191547/rss" title="try.expo.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Agentic Mobile Development, from First Prompt to the App Store&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Expo gives your coding agent the mobile infrastructure it is missing: native builds, store submits and live updates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Expo &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191548/rss" title="daverupert.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Recursion is DEAD and HTML Killed It&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A fun, practical look at using Chrome’s new out-of-order HTML streaming (known as &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191549/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;declarative partial updates&lt;/a&gt;) to let the browser assemble nested comment threads for you. Chromium-only, but exciting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dave Rupert &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;🖼️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191550/rss" title="anderegg.ca" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;I Guess I’m Using WebP Now&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — It’s been 16 years since Google introduced the WebP image format, support is now widespread (&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191551/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;97%&lt;/a&gt;), and hey, maybe they’re worth another look?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gavin Anderegg &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191552/rss" title="utilitybend.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Scroll-Triggered Animation as the Missing Piece for Scrollytelling on the Web&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A look at the CSS Animation Triggers spec, an Interop 2027 candidate, and how it kicks off an animation based on scroll position. Five demos show what it enables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brecht De Ruyte &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

