&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191553/rss" title="developer.mozilla.org" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Firefox 158 Enables JPEG XL by Default&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Coming shortly after Chrome did the same, Firefox now supports JPEG XL by default, adding &lt;code&gt;image/jxl&lt;/code&gt; to its image &lt;code&gt;Accept&lt;/code&gt; header.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mozilla &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;🌐 In other browser news, &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191554/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Chrome 156 beta is out&lt;/a&gt; (stable next week) and adds support for CSS &lt;code&gt;random()&lt;/code&gt;. Also, &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191555/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Safari Technology Preview 254 is out&lt;/a&gt; with both &lt;code&gt;calc-size()&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;interpolate-size&lt;/code&gt; support.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
